  "behavior_proved": [
    "Existing source/output and prefixed work directories are preserved; ownership is required before recursive removal.",
    "Repeat/concurrent real processes preserve separate reports; actual CLI checks only its generated summary and fails a known 50% branch result.",
    "Copied/replaced/malformed/missing ownership and PID reuse cannot authorize cleanup.",
    "Abrupt process death retains attributable work without preventing a fresh generation; real Windows file lock retains/restores ownership and reports bytes.",
    "Source/test/report-allocation failures clean eligible working copies; marker-write failure removes only still-identical empty claims and diagnoses partial ownership.",
    "Global preload teardown cleans normal completion and protects replacement directories even under explicit process exit.",
    "Linux startup-home caching is contained by a test-only OS adapter; inherited friction sentinel stays byte-identical, import forms and native child environment are exercised."
  ],
  "corrections": [
    "Historical process-exit cleanup implementation was not proof of normal Bun lifecycle behavior; B03 reproduces and repairs the gap.",
    "Initial Linux focused run failed inherited-home isolation; retained RED log precedes adapter repair.",
    "A new default-import regression exposed incomplete adapter exports; repaired before final runs.",
    "Two-run fixture exceeded default 5 seconds under concurrent checks; explicit 30-second integration limit, unchanged behavioral assertions."
  ],
